IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ta-nouns`
IMPORT `ta-logic`

-- Terrorism Act 2000, Part III, sections 21D to 21H -- layer 1: telling someone that a disclosure has been made, or that an
-- investigation is under way, when the information came to the person in the regulated sector; the exceptions; the meanings.
-- "A business in the regulated sector", "credit institution" and "supervisory authority" turn on Schedule 3A; "group" on a 2002
-- Directive; "equivalent money laundering requirements" on a 2015 Directive; none of these is among the sources, so each is a
-- fact the caller states.  Each section answers on its own (E1 option C); section 21D(5) is the one place where the offence
-- and its three exceptions are brought together, and it takes the exceptions' answers as inputs.

§ `Part III Terrorist Property -- Offences (continued): tipping off`

§§ `s 21D Tipping off: regulated sector`

-- src:348 | (2) The matters are that the person or another person has made a disclosure under a provision of this Part—
-- src:349 | (a) to a constable,
-- src:350 | (b) in accordance with a procedure established by that person's employer for the making of disclosures under that provision,
-- src:351 | (c) to a nominated officer, or
-- src:352 | (d) to a National Crime Agency officer authorised for the purposes of that provision by the Director General of that Agency,
-- src:353 | of information that came to that person in the course of a business in the regulated sector.
@ref s 21D(2) (src:348-353)
GIVEN `the matter` IS A `Protected matter facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 21D(2) the matter is within subsection (2)` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the matter`'s `the person or another person has made a disclosure under a provision of this Part`
           AND (`the matter`'s `the disclosure was made to a constable`
                OR `the matter`'s `the disclosure was made in accordance with a procedure established by that person's employer for the making of disclosures under that provision`
                OR `the matter`'s `the disclosure was made to a nominated officer`
                OR `the matter`'s `the disclosure was made to a National Crime Agency officer authorised for the purposes of that provision by the Director General of that Agency`)
           AND `the matter`'s `the disclosure was of information that came to that person in the course of a business in the regulated sector`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The matters are that the person or another person has made a disclosure under a provision of this Part"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:344 | (1) A person commits an offence if—
-- src:345 | (a) the person discloses any matter within subsection (2);
-- src:346 | (b) the disclosure is likely to prejudice any investigation that might be conducted following the disclosure referred to in that subsection; and
-- src:347 | (c) the information on which the disclosure is based came to the person in the course of a business in the regulated sector.
@ref s 21D(1) (src:344-347)
GIVEN `the matter is within subsection (2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the facts` IS A `Tipping off facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 21D(1) the person commits an offence by tipping off` IS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person commits an offence if—"
    `the conjunction` `the matter is within subsection (2)` `and also` rest
    WHERE
        prejudice MEANS `the fact` (`the facts`'s `the disclosure is likely to prejudice any investigation that might be conducted following the disclosure referred to in subsection (2)`)
        regulated MEANS `the fact` (`the facts`'s `the information on which the disclosure is based came to the person in the course of a business in the regulated sector`)
        rest MEANS `the conjunction` prejudice `and also` regulated

-- src:354 | (3) A person commits an offence if—
-- src:355 | (a) the person discloses that an investigation into allegations that an offence under this Part has been committed is being contemplated or is being carried out;
-- src:356 | (b) the disclosure is likely to prejudice that investigation; and
-- src:357 | (c) the information on which the disclosure is based came to the person in the course of a business in the regulated sector.
@ref s 21D(3) (src:354-357)
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Investigation disclosure facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 21D(3) the person commits an offence by disclosing an investigation` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the facts`'s `the person discloses that an investigation into allegations that an offence under this Part has been committed is being contemplated or is being carried out`
           AND `the facts`'s `the disclosure is likely to prejudice that investigation`
           AND `the facts`'s `the information on which the disclosure is based came to the person in the course of a business in the regulated sector`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person commits an offence if—"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:358 | (4) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable—
-- src:359 | (a) on summary conviction to imprisonment for a term not exceeding three months, or to a fine not exceeding level 5 on the standard scale, or to both;
-- src:360 | (b) on conviction on indictment to imprisonment for a term not exceeding two years, or to a fine, or to both.
@ref s 21D(4) (src:358-360)
GIVEN `the route of conviction` IS A `Conviction route`
      `level 5 on the standard scale` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Penalty ceiling`
DECIDE `s 21D(4) the ceiling of the penalty for an offence under s 21D` IS
    CONSIDER `the route of conviction`
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN `Penalty ceiling` OF 24, `No ceiling is stated`
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN `Penalty ceiling` OF 3, `A fine not exceeding` `level 5 on the standard scale`

-- src:361 | (5) This section is subject to—
-- src:362 | (a) section 21E (disclosures within an undertaking or group etc),
-- src:363 | (b) section 21F (other permitted disclosures between institutions etc), and
-- src:364 | (c) section 21G (other permitted disclosures etc).
@ref s 21D(5) (src:361-364)
GIVEN `s 21E` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 21F` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 21G` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 21D(5) an exception in s 21E, s 21F or s 21G displaces the offence` IS
    -- the three exceptions combine by the disjunction: one that applies displaces the offence; all three JUST FALSE leaves it standing; any other mixture is not covered
    `the disjunction` `s 21E` `or else` rest
    WHERE
        rest MEANS `the disjunction` `s 21F` `or else` `s 21G`

§§ `s 21E Disclosures within an undertaking or group etc`

-- src:366 | (1) An employee, officer or partner of an undertaking does not commit an offence under section 21D if the disclosure is to an employee, officer or partner of the same undertaking.
@ref s 21E(1) (src:366)
GIVEN `the discloser is an employee, officer or partner of an undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is to an employee, officer or partner of the same undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 21E(1) the person does not commit an offence under s 21D` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the discloser is an employee, officer or partner of an undertaking` AND `the disclosure is to an employee, officer or partner of the same undertaking`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not commit an offence under section 21D if the disclosure is to an employee, officer or partner of the same undertaking"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:367 | (2) A person does not commit an offence under section 21D in respect of a disclosure by a credit institution or a financial institution if—
-- src:368 | (a) the disclosure is to a credit institution or a financial institution,
-- src:369 | (b) the institution to whom the disclosure is made is situated in the United Kingdom or an EEA state or in a country or territory imposing equivalent money laundering requirements, and
-- src:370 | (c) both the institution making the disclosure and the institution to whom it is made belong to the same group.
@ref s 21E(2) (src:367-370)
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Group disclosure facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 21E(2) the person does not commit an offence under s 21D by a disclosure within a group` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the facts`'s `the disclosure is by a credit institution or a financial institution`
           AND `the facts`'s `the disclosure is to a credit institution or a financial institution`
           AND `the facts`'s `the institution to whom the disclosure is made is situated in the United Kingdom or an EEA state or in a country or territory imposing equivalent money laundering requirements`
           AND `the facts`'s `both the institution making the disclosure and the institution to whom it is made belong to the same group`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person does not commit an offence under section 21D in respect of a disclosure by a credit institution or a financial institution if—"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:371 | (3) In subsection (2) “ group ” has the same meaning as in Directive 2002/87/EC of the European Parliament and of the Council of 16 th December 2002 on the supplementary supervision of credit institutions, insurance undertakings and investment firms in a financial conglomerate.
@ref s 21E(3) (src:371)
GIVEN `the answer the Directive gives` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 21E(3) the institutions belong to the same group` IS
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "“group” has the same meaning as in Directive 2002/87/EC", which is not among the sources; with no answer from it, NOTHING
    `the answer the Directive gives`

-- src:372 | (4) A professional legal adviser or a relevant professional adviser does not commit an offence under section 21D if—
-- src:373 | (a) the disclosure is to a professional legal adviser or a relevant professional adviser,
-- src:374 | (b) both the person making the disclosure and the person to whom it is made carry on business in the United Kingdom or an EEA state or in a country or territory imposing equivalent money laundering requirements, and
-- src:375 | (c) those persons perform their professional activities within different undertakings that share common ownership, management or control.
@ref s 21E(4) (src:372-375)
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Adviser group facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 21E(4) the adviser does not commit an offence under s 21D` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the facts`'s `the person making the disclosure is a professional legal adviser or a relevant professional adviser`
           AND `the facts`'s `the disclosure is to a professional legal adviser or a relevant professional adviser`
           AND `the facts`'s `both the person making the disclosure and the person to whom it is made carry on business in the United Kingdom or an EEA state or in a country or territory imposing equivalent money laundering requirements`
           AND `the facts`'s `those persons perform their professional activities within different undertakings that share common ownership, management or control`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A professional legal adviser or a relevant professional adviser does not commit an offence under section 21D if—"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 21F Other permitted disclosures between institutions etc`

-- src:377 | (1) This section applies to a disclosure—
-- src:378 | (a) by a credit institution to another credit institution,
-- src:379 | (b) by a financial institution to another financial institution,
-- src:380 | (c) by a professional legal adviser to another professional legal adviser, or
-- src:381 | (d) by a relevant professional adviser of a particular kind to another relevant professional adviser of the same kind.
@ref s 21F(1) (src:377-381)
GIVEN `the disclosure` IS A `Between institutions facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 21F(1) this section applies to the disclosure` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the disclosure`'s `by a credit institution to another credit institution`
           OR `the disclosure`'s `by a financial institution to another financial institution`
           OR `the disclosure`'s `by a professional legal adviser to another professional legal adviser`
           OR `the disclosure`'s `by a relevant professional adviser of a particular kind to another relevant professional adviser of the same kind`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies to a disclosure—"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:382 | (2) A person does not commit an offence under section 21D in respect of a disclosure to which this section applies if—
-- src:383 | (a) the disclosure relates to—
-- src:384 | (i) a client or former client of the institution or adviser making the disclosure and the institution or adviser to whom it is made,
-- src:385 | (ii) a transaction involving them both, or
-- src:386 | (iii) the provision of a service involving them both;
-- src:387 | (b) the disclosure is for the purpose only of preventing an offence under this Part of this Act;
-- src:388 | (c) the institution or adviser to whom the disclosure is made is situated in the United Kingdom or an EEA state or in a country or territory imposing equivalent money laundering requirements; and
-- src:389 | (d) the institution or adviser making the disclosure and the institution or adviser to whom it is made are subject to equivalent duties of professional confidentiality and the protection of personal data (within the meaning of Parts 5 to 7 of the Data Protection Act 2018 (see section 3(2) and (14) of that Act)) .
@ref s 21F(2) (src:382-389)
GIVEN `section 21F applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the facts` IS A `Institution disclosure facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 21F(2) the person does not commit an offence under s 21D in respect of the disclosure` IS
    `the conjunction` `section 21F applies` `and also` rest
    WHERE
        relates MEANS `the fact` (`the facts`'s `the disclosure relates to a client or former client of the institution or adviser making the disclosure and the institution or adviser to whom it is made`
                                   OR `the facts`'s `the disclosure relates to a transaction involving them both`
                                   OR `the facts`'s `the disclosure relates to the provision of a service involving them both`)
        purpose MEANS `the fact` (`the facts`'s `the disclosure is for the purpose only of preventing an offence under this Part of this Act`)
        situated MEANS `the fact` (`the facts`'s `the institution or adviser to whom the disclosure is made is situated in the United Kingdom or an EEA state or in a country or territory imposing equivalent money laundering requirements`)
        duties MEANS `the fact` (`the facts`'s `the institution or adviser making the disclosure and the institution or adviser to whom it is made are subject to equivalent duties of professional confidentiality and the protection of personal data`)
        relatesAndPurpose MEANS `the conjunction` relates `and also` purpose
        situatedAndDuties MEANS `the conjunction` situated `and also` duties
        rest MEANS `the conjunction` relatesAndPurpose `and also` situatedAndDuties

§§ `s 21G Other permitted disclosures etc`

-- src:391 | (1) A person does not commit an offence under section 21D if the disclosure is—
-- src:392 | (a) to the authority that is the supervisory authority for that person by virtue of the Money Laundering, Terrorist Financing and Transfer of Funds (Information on the Payer) Regulations 2017; ...
-- src:393 | (aa) made in good faith by virtue of section 21CA (disclosures within the regulated sector); or
-- src:394 | (b) for the purpose of—
-- src:395 | (i) the detection, investigation or prosecution of a criminal offence (whether in the United Kingdom or elsewhere),
-- src:396 | (ii) an investigation under the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002, or
-- src:397 | (iii) the enforcement of any order of a court under that Act.
@ref s 21G(1) (src:391-397)
GIVEN `the disclosure` IS A `Permitted disclosure facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 21G(1) the person does not commit an offence under s 21D` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the disclosure`'s `the disclosure is to the authority that is the supervisory authority for that person by virtue of the Money Laundering, Terrorist Financing and Transfer of Funds (Information on the Payer) Regulations 2017`
           OR `the disclosure`'s `the disclosure is made in good faith by virtue of s 21CA`
           OR `the disclosure`'s `the disclosure is for the purpose of the detection, investigation or prosecution of a criminal offence (whether in the United Kingdom or elsewhere)`
           OR `the disclosure`'s `the disclosure is for the purpose of an investigation under the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002`
           OR `the disclosure`'s `the disclosure is for the purpose of the enforcement of any order of a court under that Act`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person does not commit an offence under section 21D if the disclosure is—"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:398 | (2) A professional legal adviser or a relevant professional adviser does not commit an offence under section 21D if the disclosure—
-- src:399 | (a) is to the adviser's client, and
-- src:400 | (b) is made for the purpose of dissuading the client from engaging in conduct amounting to an offence.
@ref s 21G(2) (src:398-400)
GIVEN `the person is a professional legal adviser or a relevant professional adviser` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the disclosure is to the adviser's client` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is made for the purpose of dissuading the client from engaging in conduct amounting to an offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 21G(2) the adviser does not commit an offence under s 21D` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person is a professional legal adviser or a relevant professional adviser`
           AND `the disclosure is to the adviser's client`
           AND `it is made for the purpose of dissuading the client from engaging in conduct amounting to an offence`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A professional legal adviser or a relevant professional adviser does not commit an offence under section 21D if the disclosure—"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:401 | (3) A person does not commit an offence under section 21D(1) if the person does not know or suspect that the disclosure is likely to have the effect mentioned in section 21D(1)(b).
@ref s 21G(3) (src:401)
GIVEN `the person knows or suspects that the disclosure is likely to have the effect mentioned in s 21D(1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 21G(3) the person does not commit an offence under s 21D(1)` IS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the person knows or suspects that the disclosure is likely to have the effect mentioned in s 21D(1)(b)`)
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person does not commit an offence under section 21D(1) if the person does not know or suspect that the disclosure is likely to have the effect"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:402 | (4) A person does not commit an offence under section 21D(3) if the person does not know or suspect that the disclosure is likely to have the effect mentioned in section 21D(3)(b).
@ref s 21G(4) (src:402)
GIVEN `the person knows or suspects that the disclosure is likely to have the effect mentioned in s 21D(3)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 21G(4) the person does not commit an offence under s 21D(3)` IS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the person knows or suspects that the disclosure is likely to have the effect mentioned in s 21D(3)(b)`)
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person does not commit an offence under section 21D(3) if the person does not know or suspect that the disclosure is likely to have the effect"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

§§ `s 21H Interpretation of sections 21D to 21G`

