    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): Schedule 3A decides what is a supervisory authority and is not among the sources; with no answer from it, NOTHING
    `the answer Schedule 3A gives`

-- src:408 | (2) In those sections—
-- src:409 | “ credit institution ” has the same meaning as in Schedule 3A;
@ref s 21H(2) credit institution (src:408-409)
GIVEN `the answer Schedule 3A gives` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 21H(2) the undertaking is a credit institution` IS
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "“credit institution” has the same meaning as in Schedule 3A", which is not among the sources; with no answer from it, NOTHING
    `the answer Schedule 3A gives`

-- src:408 | (2) In those sections—
-- src:410 | “ financial institution ” means an undertaking that carries on a business in the regulated sector by virtue of any of paragraphs (b) to (i) of paragraph 1(1) of that Schedule.
@ref s 21H(2) financial institution (src:408) (src:410)
GIVEN `the undertaking carries on a business in the regulated sector by virtue of any of paragraphs (b) to (i) of paragraph 1(1) of Schedule 3A` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 21H(2) the undertaking is a financial institution` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the undertaking carries on a business in the regulated sector by virtue of any of paragraphs (b) to (i) of paragraph 1(1) of Schedule 3A` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“financial institution” means an undertaking that carries on a business in the regulated sector by virtue of any of paragraphs (b) to (i) of paragraph 1(1) of that Schedule."
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:411 | (3) References in those sections to a disclosure by or to a credit institution or a financial institution include disclosure by or to an employee, officer or partner of the institution acting on its behalf.
@ref s 21H(3) (src:411)
GIVEN `the disclosure is by or to an employee, officer or partner of the institution acting on its behalf` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 21H(3) the disclosure counts as a disclosure by or to the institution` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the disclosure is by or to an employee, officer or partner of the institution acting on its behalf` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "References in those sections to a disclosure by or to a credit institution or a financial institution include disclosure by or to an employee, officer or partner of the institution acting on its behalf."
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:412 | (4) For the purposes of those sections a country or territory imposes “equivalent money laundering requirements” if it imposes requirements equivalent to those laid down in Directive 2015/849/EU of the European Parliament and of the Council of 20th May 2015 on the prevention of the use of the financial system for the purpose of money laundering and terrorist financing, as amended by Directive 2018/843 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 30th May 2018.
@ref s 21H(4) (src:412)
GIVEN `the country or territory imposes requirements equivalent to those laid down in Directive 2015/849/EU, as amended by Directive 2018/843` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 21H(4) the country or territory imposes equivalent money laundering requirements` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the country or territory imposes requirements equivalent to those laid down in Directive 2015/849/EU, as amended by Directive 2018/843` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a country or territory imposes “equivalent money laundering requirements” if it imposes requirements equivalent to those laid down in Directive 2015/849/EU"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:413 | (5) In those sections “ relevant professional adviser ” means an accountant, auditor or tax adviser who is a member of a professional body which is established for accountants, auditors or tax advisers (as the case may be) and which makes provision for—
-- src:414 | (a) testing the competence of those seeking admission to membership of such a body as a condition for such admission; and
-- src:415 | (b) imposing and maintaining professional and ethical standards for its members, as well as imposing sanctions for non-compliance with those standards.
@ref s 21H(5) (src:413-415)
GIVEN `the person` IS A `Professional adviser facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 21H(5) the person is a relevant professional adviser` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person`'s `an accountant, auditor or tax adviser`
           AND `the person`'s `a member of a professional body established for accountants, auditors or tax advisers (as the case may be)`
           AND `the person`'s `the body makes provision for testing the competence of those seeking admission to membership as a condition for admission`
           AND `the person`'s `the body makes provision for imposing and maintaining professional and ethical standards for its members, and sanctions for non-compliance`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“relevant professional adviser” means an accountant, auditor or tax adviser who is a member of a professional body"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE
